	Introduction, Preface

	Quest (Questionary Helper) was from the begining developed and
	spread for the first time 06-07-92 and was the first Quest door
	for the /X package. I am very disapointed that people from the
	scene tries to steal my name, like the AFL Quest program which
	actually even does about the same things as my program.
	Anyway this new version V1.10 was developed to fit inside the
	Account ED package so you now can look at your users and edit
	faster than ever. All sysop commands in the previous Quest doors
	has been removed and the old source has got some new and faster
	routines. There are also several new functions which I've
	included to this version more about them later. From now on Quest
	will be shipped together with every new version of Account ED, BUT
	if there comes any updates on Quest before a new Account ED package
	is released, then Quest will be spread as normal with the file
	name QST-VXXX where XXX is the version number.

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	What will Quest do for you?

	Quest let's you skip your Script14400 files and the Answers file
	which to many sysop give them a hard headace.. I think you know
	what I mean when you've got 4 new users and then you should
	update them, phew what a booring job.. Load your answers file
	into CED and then go to the bottom of a 200kb large file!

	Well, forget that then you have Account ED & Quest, which are
	the perfect couple.. Quest let's your users answer to all questions
	you prefer and then stores their answers separately in the QuestApp
	directory. If you then wanna look at any applications you just
	search for that user in the Account Editor and then press the / key
	and you will then immidiately have that users application on your
	screen. If it concerns new user you just use the Scan for New Users
	function in the Account Editor and you will both see the users
	account and the questionary!! That's what I call powerfull!
	You can even print the users questionary if you like to!

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	Instalation ..

	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/BBS.Cmd file:

	*QUEST    Rm005Doors:Arexx/Account/Quest.rexx

	You should then use the MCI commands to envoke Quest and I
	recommend that you first in your BBS:Node(x)/Joined.txt file
	adds this line:

	~CC_QUEST

	Which will automatically start quest then a user has given his
	phone number and so on!
	
	When you have managed to do that it would be time to move the
	Account ED & Quest package to your Doors:Arexx/ path, which is
	the path all my doors requires so you better not put it elsewhere.

	After doing that you should edit the AccEd.Presets file which
	is the main configuration file for Account ED & Quest.

	| Recieve App Mail | Delusion           | Print Account    |   On |                  |
	| AccountED Colour | [0m               | Search New Users |  300 |                  |
	| Log Status AccED | 4                  | Members Conf     |    5 |                  |
	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Kickout After X  |    5 |------------------|
	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Questionary      |    4 | AccountED © 1993 |
	| AutoAccess Quest | No                 | MustEnter No Ret |  Yes | Delusion of VTL! |
	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	At the end of that file you will find the above. Here is what it
	means..

	Recieve App Mail - is the person who gets the message from the new user
	Kickout After X  - drops carrier on a user who has pressed return on 5
			   or more questions in the questionary
	Questionary	 - Is which number on the questionary which it will
			   question from. They are located in the QuestQst dir
	AutoAccess Quest - It will automatically give a new user access after
			   answering the questions. It will use the first preset
			   in the preset file and give that access to the new
			   user so he could upload and thing like that.
			   If you wan't to use this function choose YES otherwise
			   just enter NO
	MustEnter No Ret - If this is set to YES a user can't pres return on
			   a questions becouse there will come up a text that
			   says you may not do so and ask the question again.
			   However if you wan't to use the kickout after X
			   function you have to set this one to NO.

	That was all that concerned Quest, but remember that the first preset
	in this file is used to give new users access if you have choosed
	auto acess! Example file is included in the archive.

  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _
 /  \/
	How to set up the Questions file

	Old users of Quest should also read this, it's completly different!

	As you may be familiar to the MCI commands inside /X I've created
	something that looks the same, but in a reverse mode if you could
	say so. Before every question you can give these command:

	~	- Just question that question
	        - Nothing, means it's a comment and will only be displayed
	~N	- It tells Account ED that the users real name is asked
	~A	- Tells that it's the users address being asked, note that
		  you can have 2 such commands after each other so you could
		  ask the adress on 2 lines
	~C	- Tells that you are asking for the users country
	~V	- Tells that you are asking for the users Voice Phone Number
	~D	- Tells that you are asking for the users Data  Phone Number
	~S	- Tells that you are asking for the users Sex & Age
	~P	- Tells that you are asking for the users Social Security Code
	~U	- Tells that you are asking for what the users does with his
		  computer and such things.
	~W	- Tells that you are asking for from where he got you phone #
	~R	- Works like the ~A command in the way that you could use two
		  questions with a ~R before so the user could give two lines
		  with reasons why you should let him into you BBS

	An example questionary is included. The questionary is originally
	designed by The Silencer / Equinox, but slightly remade by Delusion!

	Anyway you now might wonder why you should tell the Questionary program
	what you intend to ask and such things, well it's very simple!
	In comming versions of Account ED it should be possible to both get
	the users Account and the most essintial infomation from the questionary
	on the screen at the same time, like the users name and social security
	code. I have NOT coded that feature in Account ED yet, but it will
	very soon come. So here is your chance to be one step ahead :) so you
	will have it working as soon as the new Account ED arrives.

	In older versions of Quest you could choose to save the users answers
	with questions and answers or answers alone. Becouse of the above said
	new features the questions and answers format doesn't work so there
	for that function has been removed and you can only save the answers.
	Account ED still supports the both formats so you can view older
	questionaries, but you have to the ~X commands to your old questionaries
	if you have some in your Doors:Arexx/Quest/Questions direcotry and copy
	them into the Doors:Arexx/Account/QuestQST dir. As you may have guessed
	the function with diplaying info in Account Ed will not work on old
	questionaries which is in the form Questions - Answers. I will maybe
	fix a converter util for that.

	Note that all commands has to be two chars, if you only have a ~ on
	a question it should look like "~ " and if you have a two chars command
	it should look like "~N" for instance. This goes for the space command
	too which would look like "  ", remeber that you should NOT write the
	" " before and after it's only so you could see what I mean.

	In otherwords this means that all questions should start on column 3
	and in column 1 and 2 there should be the commands!

